    {
      "id": "aAsoWemQZlE7papkawmrv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 268.8833336830139,
      "y": 699.5,
      "width": 784.9166870117188,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 21220072,
      "version": 398,
      "versionNonce": 1728451048,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793190279476,
      "created": 1793190159344,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TRAIN TIME VS TEST TIME COMPUTE\n\npeople used to follow this steps to increase the model accuracy and performnce:\n- increase the model size ( the number of parameters)\n- increase the dataset used for training \n- improve gpu flop [still needed :)]\n\nhowever this does not scale well and that why we focus on test time compute.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TRAIN TIME VS TEST TIME COMPUTE\n\npeople used to follow this steps to increase the model accuracy and performnce:\n- increase the model size ( the number of parameters)\n- increase the dataset used for training \n- improve gpu flop [still needed :)]\n\nhowever this does not scale well and that why we focus on test time compute.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pYQgx1UNYje_GyOqZXx0V",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 254.88333368301392,
      "y": 933.5,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aa",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1258488216,
      "version": 126,
      "versionNonce": 806066840,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793190425621,
      "created": 1793190397372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "test time compute focus on scaling inference instead of pre-training and post\ntraining compute. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "test time compute focus on scaling inference instead of pre-training and post training compute. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UgMUFmtKUdjsA2A7shJJx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 267.8833336830139,
      "y": 979.5,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ab",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 691314622,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 167921726,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793255611351,
      "created": 1793255609914,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\nThe relationship between a model’s scale (e.g., compute, dataset size, and\nparameter counts) and its performance is described by scaling laws. They often\ntake the form of power laws, where increasing one variable (e.g., compute) leads\nto a proportional change in another (e.g., performance).\n\nIn these power laws, these relationships tend to follow diminishing returns: each\ndoubling of compute gives smaller gains than the previous doubling.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\nThe relationship between a model’s scale (e.g., compute, dataset size, and parameter counts) and its performance is described by scaling laws. They often take the form of power laws, where increasing one variable (e.g., compute) leads to a proportional change in another (e.g., performance).\n\nIn these power laws, these relationships tend to follow diminishing returns: each doubling of compute gives smaller gains than the previous doubling.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ijldaN7zzX67wikILN8ab",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 272.8833336830139,
      "y": 1212.5,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ac",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1520730530,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1613602978,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793255668076,
      "created": 1793255665525,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When plotted on regular axes, this creates a curve that flattens out. But when\nboth axes are put on a log-log scale, the power-law relationship becomes a\nstraight line, making trends easier to see and compare across many orders of\nmagnitude\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When plotted on regular axes, this creates a curve that flattens out. But when both axes are put on a log-log scale, the power-law relationship becomes a straight line, making trends easier to see and compare across many orders of magnitude\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
